Dubinin–Radushkevich (D–R) isotherm is usually employed to explain the adsorption mechanism with respect to Gaussian energy distribution onto a heterogeneous surface and determine the adsorption nature as physical or chemical based on the mean free energy (E)60. The D–R isotherm model is expressed by Eq. (3). Model parameters ε, β and E can be determined and calculated by Eqs. (4) and (5).3\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
